{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536043-first-shovelheads","id":1536043,"title":"First Shovelheads","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-21T00:47:00-07:00","id":1536043,"title":"First Shovelheads","content":"Hi I have two questions:<br /> <br /> When and where did the Sabbat start with the praxis of massembracing shovelheads?<br /> <br /> Where massembraces already before the founding of the sect used as a strategy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T12:06:02-07:00","id":1536075,"title":"","content":"I don't think there is any canonical answer. It's possible to reconstruct the timeline using clues in canon, but it's important to remember that the history of the Sabbat has changed throughout editions. Much of the lore that was created for the Dark Ages and Revised editions don't reflect what was previously established. For example, in the original sourcebooks of the Sabbat, it was mentioned how critical and important was the involvement of the Ravnos Methusaleh Vestgeir in the 1500s and1600s in establishing the sect. This character isn't even mentioned in the Revised books I own. He seems to be forgotten even though the belief that Vestgeir was actually Caine is fundamental to the sect and the Path of Caine. Furthermore, originally the Sabbat Paths of Enlightenment were only created some time after the Convention of Thorns. But the Dark Ages line retconned many of them as existing prior to the Anarch Revolt. <br /> <br /> So depending on which edition's lore you prefer, you can come to different conclusions. Many people seem to want the Sabbat to form exactly as we know it today five seconds after the Convention of Thorns was signed. Instead I think it was a slow process by which the hold outs of the Anarch Revolt established their own sect called the Sabbat, and how the Sabbat we recognize today actually formed (which is different in many respects from how the Sabbat was originally).<br /> <br /> We know from Chicago By Night that Philippe Rigaud was embraced in 1673 in what was obviously a shovelhead ceremony. It had to have started before then. So the time when it started to occur was probably between 1500-1650. We don't have any evidence that shovelhead embraces were performed during the Anarch Revolt that I know of (and if there are, I suspect it's a late Revised era addition that I would ignore). This seems to be an innovation of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> So when did the remaining Anarchs become Sabbat? Well, it's probably when Vestgeir became its main leader. I imagine these was an initial period of several decades where the Camarilla destroyed many of the remaining Anarchs, and when Vestgeir first appeared he began creating the actual sect of the Sabbat from the remaining Anarchs who were desperate to survive. Many of the unique institutions of the sect were probably first introduced by Vestgeir. While the Vaulderie was of course known before this, I suspect the process of constantly performing it among coteries happened at this time in an attempt to prevent future betrayals of Anarchs deciding it was better to join the Camarilla. It also makes sense that mass embraces to make up their depleted numbers began at this time. So for me, I would pick a time period of 1550-1600 as to when this first began, and it probably took some time before the Creation Rites became standard practice throughout the sect. For my own personal taste, I would pick a time in the latter half of that period.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T12:54:14-07:00","id":1536076,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> 100% regarding their view of Sabbat history after the Convention of Thorns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T14:21:05-07:00","id":1536082,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if it actually predates the Sabbat, and was a tactic pre-sect Tzims used. I could easily see ancient Tzims making masses of childer at the same time they were making vozhds and specialized ghouls and just plain old summoning swarms of mundane animals. If they had a Cappadocian on the payroll, zombies as well. To fight a Tzim has always been to face a nightmarish swarm of everything a vampire can create.<br /> <br /> The early Sabbat would have mostly lacked the ability to create vozhds and zombies, but they could bust into someone's house and turn a family into vaulderied vamps. The mass embrace was likely the one ability of their elders that any young Sabbat could mimic. So mimic they did.<br /> <br /> I doubt they even thought of it as a &quot;Sabbat tactic&quot; at first. It was just, the Voivode on the hill used this this this this and this tactic, the neonate Tzims grew up seeing it, so they adopted the one tactic they could as dirt-poor rebels sleeping in holes in the ground.<br /> <br /> It was only as the practice spread far beyond Tzim lands that it started to be viewed as &quot;Sabbat tactic&quot;, rather than just young poor Tzims adopting the one tactic of their elders that was still available to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T23:57:33-07:00","id":1536145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536043-first-shovelheads?p=1536082#post1536082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be surprised if it actually predates the Sabbat, and was a tactic pre-sect Tzims used. I could easily see ancient Tzims making masses of childer at the same time they were making vozhds and specialized ghouls and just plain old summoning swarms of mundane animals. If they had a Cappadocian on the payroll, zombies as well. To fight a Tzim has always been to face a nightmarish swarm of everything a vampire can create.<br /> <br /> The early Sabbat would have mostly lacked the ability to create vozhds and zombies, but they could bust into someone's house and turn a family into vaulderied vamps. The mass embrace was likely the one ability of their elders that any young Sabbat could mimic. So mimic they did.<br /> <br /> I doubt they even thought of it as a &quot;Sabbat tactic&quot; at first. It was just, the Voivode on the hill used this this this this and this tactic, the neonate Tzims grew up seeing it, so they adopted the one tactic they could as dirt-poor rebels sleeping in holes in the ground.<br /> <br /> It was only as the practice spread far beyond Tzim lands that it started to be viewed as &quot;Sabbat tactic&quot;, rather than just young poor Tzims adopting the one tactic of their elders that was still available to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> I would go further, and say the Mass Embrace, as a tactic of war-making, has been around basically as long as vampires have. Or at least as long as the Second City. It's a potent tool, if you need a lot of power very quickly.<br /> <br /> It's just never been what one might call common, aside from the aforementioned Tzimisce elders. The upsides to creating a load of fledgling vampires runs up against the downsides of creating a load of fledgling vampires. Those that survive the cannon fodder stage become nuisances, burdens, or rivals unto themselves. Those vampires who are already on the backfoot or want to gain (or keep) a foothold may mass embrace situationally. Whereas those well established and entrenched in their domain may be wary of producing a ton of &quot;new blood&quot;.<br /> <br /> (See New York City after the Camarilla took it over during the transition to Revised as one example. Where they reluctantly dipped into mass embraces to take and hold the city, and needed to avoid stepping on the toes of some Clans over others. Most were Nosferatu, Gangrel, and Brujah, because no one wanted a bunch of new Ventrue, Tremere, or Toreadors in the areas, as rivals or to bolster some political blocs over others.)<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce had a lot of other tools, as demonstrated above. Moreover, they were masters of the Blood Bond. Ergo, they were more willing to do the occasional mass embrace, if it meant holding onto their territory. Tzimisce were also just notoriously belligerent, against rivals within and outside the Clan. So the Fiends had no shortage of wars in which to spend the lives of surplus Childer. (Which, of course, ends up fostering resentment that created the Anarch Revolt in the first place. The nascent Sabbat learned well from their Elders).<br /> <br /> The ancient Baali, I think, probably also used mass embraces for some of the same reasons as the Sabbat. It's part of why the Baali Wars were such a threat in antiquity. They not only had demons and magic, they also had no compunction about kidnapping entire villages and throwing them against their enemies.<br /> <br /> (Which, in turn, my explain why other Clans would consider the practice unwholesome, or at least dangerous. Their Methuselahs remember well when the Baali invaded their lands in droves. Swarming them, both figuratively and literally (in the form of insects or vermin).)<br /> <br /> What makes the Sabbat different than most of Kindred affairs is their willingness to employ shovelheads as a first recourse, rather than a last resort. Turning the Sabbat from merely rebellious Childer who could be brought to heel (theoretically), to a walking, talking, politically active viral outbreak. Flaring up seemingly at random.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T12:51:39-07:00","id":1536162,"title":"","content":"I don't think mass embraces make much sense prior to the vaulderie. There's no reason why the suddenly hungry mob of newly created vampires wouldn't attack their creator for any number of reasons including hunger, disorientation, etc. After all, new childer are not automatically loyal. Being alone, the individual vampire could be overwhelmed by the sheer numbers. Plus it's a lot of blood for a single vampire to create mass embraces in a short time.<br /> <br /> But if you have a pack and are performing the vaulderie where everyone equally contributes blood, and the mass victims are fed from that, it's easier on the blood resources of each individual vampire, and you have something that creates some kind of initial loyalty or fondness from their vinculum to prevent attacks on you. Plus you're not alone and have allies around you just in case something goes wrong and the embraced masses do attack you.<br /> <br /> As for the Tzimisce, prior to the Anarch Revolt, they were aristocratic, individualistic, territorial, and exclusive. The ideal is Dracula and his small brood of brides, not hordes of unreliable childer. If a Tzimisce elder wants disposable canon fodder, she uses ghouls, Revenants, or other servants. That is what they are for. You don't waste blood on someone you think would be an unworthy childe.<br /> <br /> (This gets into another point that drives me crazy with some players - I don't think new vampires have much in the way of powers, the standard character creation process of 3 or 4 dots of Disciplines reflects what a vampire who has progressed from fledgling to neonate has accomplished, it's not some rule that the first night of the embrace every vampire has them.)<br /> <br /> Now I could believe that surviving Anarch Tzimisce, who have rejected the ways of their elders, might be the first to see potential in the new tactic and propagate it, maybe even invent it simply because of the creepy terror factor. But it's not something I see their elders doing. And of course, if we want to go with &quot;canon&quot; (with the usual caveats of <i>which</i> canon to use), there seems to be no evidence this tactic as ever used prior to the Sabbat, certainly not pre-Anarch Revolt (at least that I know of, but we have an entire edition out now I've never read).<br /> <br /> Could some vampire in a desperate situation suddenly embrace many childer in one night to create an instant army and rely on their Disciplines to keep control of them all? It is certainly possible and probably has been done by some vampires over the course of thousands of years of history. But I don't consider that to be the same as anything like the Sabbat creation rites, or anything that would be part of Tzimisce clan culture. Certainly any vampire that used this strategy would immediately cause every other vampire in the local area ally in order to destroy her and discourage any such attempts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T13:24:10-07:00","id":1536165,"title":"","content":"I mostly agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> here. It seems like a simple tactic, but its repercussions are many and complex.<br /> <br /> As I see it, the ratio of vampires to mortals went down through history, which means the further you go in the past, the more blood was at a premium, even if the Masquerade wasn't a problem.<br /> <br /> Embracing an entire village? Even if you manage to completely reuse their blood, how many extra mortals you need simply to have this army battle-ready for more than a single night? Not to mention control.<br /> <br /> The Vaulderie is key to make mass embrace into a reliable tactic, and its blood cost is too heavy even then if you want the fledglings to be minimally more capable than mortals. Despite being done on enemy territory, doing it on small populations would at most get you a Pyrrhic victory after their frenzied feast.<br /> <br /> So, all in all, I think the tactic as a regular thing isn't even as old as the Sabbat, though it surely may have seen some use during the Anarch Revolt and very rarely before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T11:31:50-07:00","id":1536268,"title":"","content":"Yes I can't see mass embraces being used all that much in the past before the rise of the sects as to many kindred would tax resources as the Cappadocians learned in the Dark Ages and there leadership did the Feast of Folly to cull the poorly considered childer that didn't fit the ethos of the clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T13:52:41-07:00","id":1536639,"title":"","content":"I thought it was a tactic during the first Anarch Revolt as it's simple, easy, and effective if you don't give a shit about the Masquerade or the people you kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T13:55:42-07:00","id":1536641,"title":"","content":"Even the Sabbat leadership despite there disdain for humans know enough to keep mass embraces to a low level and choose folks that won't be missed or expected to survive the upcoming battles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T04:49:02-07:00","id":1536794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1536043-first-shovelheads?p=1536641#post1536641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the Sabbat leadership despite there disdain for humans know enough to keep mass embraces to a low level and choose folks that won't be missed or expected to survive the upcoming battles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. It can be assumed, unless they're really irresponsible, that every vampire who has employed a mass Embrace throughout history intends for most, if not all, of the fledglings to die very quickly. (When they don't, which must happen on occasion, that's when the trouble starts. Which, in turn, reminds other vampires why the mass Embrace is a bad idea.)<br /> <br /> The Sabbat basically build their sect around the idea of high attrition that sculpts their population to Darwinian ends. Those shovelheads that are &quot;unfit&quot; inevitably perish (or escape and run off to make an unlife in the territory they're invading, thereby being the problem of the Sabbat's enemies). Those that are &quot;fit&quot; join the sect as &quot;True&quot; Sabbat, often replacing those existing pack members who ALSO likely die during the crusade.<br /> <br /> Ensuring there's a constant churn of low-powered licks, that don't last long enough to become a real challenge to Sabbat Elders. Those that DO survive into Ancillae-hood are vanishingly few, and can be molded by their Elders into useful tools (because they have fewer peers of equal power).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T09:56:35-07:00","id":1536803,"title":"","content":"That's certainly fits the Lasombra edicts in a nutshell Bluecho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T16:11:40-07:00","id":1536817,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the Sabbat not being as cautious as they should be is a good argument for why the Second Inquisition exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-04T16:52:43-07:00","id":1536821,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat certainly takes the Masquerade to its very edge with there actions. Most likely that the few survivors of note are given painful remainders of why discretion is needed if want to continue to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T04:47:53-07:00","id":1536887,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat could afford to be so flagrant, because they usually did so far into Camarilla territory. Let the Ivory Tower exhaust its resources and time covering up Masquerade breaches. Makes them easier to conquer. And, as I stated earlier, if some shovelheads survive into the wild, that's just more headaches for the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> When the Sabbat are in their own territory, they're far more careful. Generally this is <i>the Sabbat's</i> version of &quot;careful&quot;, so there's a lot more bodies. But still, the Sabbat practices a &quot;don't shit where you eat&quot; mentality. Mass Embraces are a tactic used on crusades for a reason. It's not for everynight &quot;recruitment&quot;. Packs must, by necessity, be more choosey about who and how they Embrace, when it's their own territory.<br /> <br /> If they aren't...well, whether there's a Second Inquisition or not, this is how you get hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}